+# Accessibility test matrix (Stage 1B, R-14 stays open)
+
+**Status: R-14 is open.** NOCTIS does not claim comprehensive accessibility support. What exists today is partial and is listed below exactly: two settings have code behind them (Button Shapes for text-only buttons, Smart Invert for the two share-card previews), Reduce Motion is read in 108 places (source count, behaviour not run), and the rest is unsupported or unverified. Nothing in this matrix was run on a device. "Simulator" means the iPhone 18 Pro simulator with the setting set through `simctl` or the system preference, screenshots viewed.
+
+Legend for "Today": **code + tested** (a unit or render test exists and passed), **code, screenshots** (viewed on the simulator), **source only** (read in the code, not run), **none** (no code reads the setting; not run).
+
+| Setting | What it asks of the app | Today | Evidence in the repository | To do before the claim can be made |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **VoiceOver** | Every control labelled, read in a sensible order, focus lands on a sheet and returns, no hidden content reachable behind the privacy cover | source only; the traversal test is written and was never run on a final build | `QA_LEDGER.md` 3.7; labels in the screens | Run the traversal test; a manual pass on onboarding, Home, Sleep, Recovery, Insights, Coach, Tonight, wind-down, alarm, Sounds, Settings, Subscription (free, premium, grace, payment problem), Paywall, share sheets, Data management (including the unfinished-deletion notice), the privacy cover, and the Watch pages; confirm the Button Shapes underline is not announced (it is an underline on the text itself, so nothing extra exists to announce) |
+| **Dynamic Type** (default, AX3, AX5) | No clipping, no overlap, 44 pt targets, long text scrolls | code, screenshots for the Subscription page (free and payment problem), Paywall and Home at AX5; 18 to 26 earlier layout rows still "fixed in source, not re-photographed" | `Docs/evidence/stage1b/screenshots/` (AX5 pairs) and `QA_LEDGER.md` | Re-run the existing screenshot suite at AX3 and AX5 on SE-sized and Pro Max-sized simulators for every screen and every widget family, and close or reopen each ledger row from a viewed image |
+| **Button Shapes** | Text-only buttons carry a shape or underline | code + tested for the text-only buttons listed below; **not** for icon-only buttons; system buttons already shaped by the system | `ButtonShapeTests` (8 render tests: off is pixel-identical, on underlines in the text's colour, wrapped text underlines line by line, no clipping); screenshots Subscription page and Paywall, base against after | Decide for icon-only custom buttons (back, close, `NightIconButton`): they look unchanged with the setting on. Covered text-only buttons: `NoctisTextButton`, `OnboardingSecondaryButton`, the Paywall free-plan link and Restore, the wind-down End. Not screenshotted: wind-down End, onboarding secondary buttons |
+| **Smart Invert** | Pictures are not inverted | code for bitmaps: the only `Image(uiImage:)` are the two share-card previews, both opt out (full search of `Packages`, `App`, `Widgets`, `Watch`) | `SmartInvertTests` (source scan) | Look at both share sheets with Smart Invert on, and decide whether the dark SwiftUI chrome inverted is acceptable (it is inverted by design) |
+| **Differentiate Without Color** | Colour is never the only signal | none: no shipped code reads `accessibilityDifferentiateWithoutColor` (only the QA probe) | a sample of a few files found no colour-only meaning; a sample is not a result | A full inventory of every colour-coded indicator (Recovery ring arcs, stage ribbons, week bars, range words, widget rings, Watch complications) and the setting on, screenshots viewed; add a non-colour twin only where one is missing |
+| **Bold Text** | Layout survives heavier text | none (system fonts adapt; no custom font was checked for a weight fallback) | `legibilityWeight` is read only by the probe | Screenshots with Bold Text on: fixed-height rows, tab bar, widgets, Watch pages; search for `Font.custom` |
+| **Increase Contrast** | Higher-contrast colours | source only: `colorSchemeContrast` read in 8 places; palette ratio tests exist | `BandStyleContrastTests`, `NoctisAppContrastTests`, `NoctisPaperContrastTests`, `WelcomeContrastTests` | Confirm the tests assert the increased-contrast variants (not confirmed); screenshots with the setting on |
+| **Reduce Transparency** | Opaque fallback for translucent surfaces | none: one `glassEffect` and the tab bar's material, system-handled; custom scrims unchecked | `accessibilityReduceTransparency` read only by the probe | Screenshots with the setting on for the tab bar, sheets, the privacy cover, widget backgrounds; add an opaque fallback only where text sits on a translucent fill and contrast drops |
+| **On/Off Labels** | Switches show I/O marks | none checked: native `Toggle` shows them automatically; custom switch-like controls were not inventoried | none | Search for custom toggles; screenshots of Settings with the setting on |
+| **Reduce Motion** | Replace or remove animation | source only: read in 108 places | `accessibilityReduceMotion` reads | Run Breathing, Meditation, sleep sounds, wind-down, the intro washes and the Watch breathing session with the setting on and watch each |
+
+## Required combinations
+
+- Each setting alone, then with Dark, then with AX5.
+- Button Shapes on at AX5: the Paywall footer links already overlap each other and the medical notice in the base build (see R-21 in the review); this is a pre-existing layout problem the setting exposes, recorded and not changed here.
+- VoiceOver with the Data management "needs attention" notice shown, and with the Subscription "payment problem" state.
+
